From d28e816a99acb6b5453095ab9d89a746f092442d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tendai Makumire <121951760+tmakumire@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Feb 2025 13:12:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add support for booting IMDT SOM8550 in Linux (#7)

Add support for booting IMDT SBC8550 in Linux
To allow our board to boot without crashing
we had to remove the kernel drivers related to
the charger PMIC (PM8550B). We had support
from Qualcomm whilst making these changes.

I have also added a new feature to the repeater I2C
so that it requires no I2C Read/Writes. This was more
useful for another project where the eUSB2 repeater
was connected to I2C pins that weren't useable in Linux.
I can probably remove this change once I prove that APPS_I2C
is working with the eUSB repeater. For now I'll keep it here.
